{"text":"purananuru","n":219,"lines":["உள்ளாற்றுக் கவலைப் புள்ளி நீழல்","முழூஉ வள்ளுரம் உணக்கும் மள்ள","புலவுதி மாதோ நீயே","பலரால் அத்தை நின் குறிஇருந் தோரே"],"tr":["uḷḷāṟṟuk kavalaip puḷḷi nīḻal","muḻūu vaḷḷuram uṇakkum maḷḷa","pulavuti mātō nīyē","palarāl attai niṉ kuṟiirun tōrē"],"colophon":{"tinai":"potuviyal","tinai_ta":"பொதுவியல்","turai_ta":"கையறுநிலை","poet_ta":"பெருஞ்கருவூர்ப்சதுக்கத்துப் பூதநாதனார்","addressed_ta":"கோப்பெருஞ் சோழன்","poet_tr":"Peruñkaruvūrpcatukkattup Pūtanātaṉār"},"scan":{"meter":"nēricai āciriyappā","ok":true,"checks":[{"name":"lines","ok":true,"detail":"4 lines"},{"name":"feet per line","ok":true,"detail":"3×4, 1×3 feet"},{"name":"foot types","ok":true,"detail":"iyaṟcīr 13, veṇcīr 2"},{"name":"linkage","ok":true,"detail":"āciriyattaḷai 7, veṇṭaḷai 5, kalittaḷai 2"},{"name":"ending","ok":true,"detail":"ends on ஏ"}],"ending":"ஏ","lines":[[{"text":"உள்ளாற்றுக்","tr":"uḷḷāṟṟuk","foot":"tēmāṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"உள்","tr":"uḷ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளாற்","tr":"ḷāṟ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றுக்","tr":"ṟuk"}]},{"text":"கவலைப்","tr":"kavalaip","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"கவ","tr":"kava"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"லைப்","tr":"laip"}]},{"text":"புள்ளி","tr":"puḷḷi","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"புள்","tr":"puḷ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளி","tr":"ḷi"}]},{"text":"நீழல்","tr":"nīḻal","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"நீ","tr":"nī"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ழல்","tr":"ḻal"}]}],[{"text":"முழூஉ","tr":"muḻūu","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"முழூ","tr":"muḻū"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"உ","tr":"u"}]},{"text":"வள்ளுர","tr":"vaḷḷura","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"வள்","tr":"vaḷ"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"ளுர","tr":"ḷura"}]},{"text":"முணக்கும்","tr":"muṇakkum","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"முணக்","tr":"muṇak"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கும்","tr":"kum"}]},{"text":"மள்ள","tr":"maḷḷa","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"மள்","tr":"maḷ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ள","tr":"ḷa"}]}],[{"text":"புலவுதி","tr":"pulavuti","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"புல","tr":"pula"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"வுதி","tr":"vuti"}]},{"text":"மாதோ","tr":"mātō","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"மா","tr":"mā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"தோ","tr":"tō"}]},{"text":"நீயே","tr":"nīyē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"நீ","tr":"nī"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யே","tr":"yē"}]}],[{"text":"பலரா","tr":"palarā","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"பல","tr":"pala"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ரா","tr":"rā"}]},{"text":"லத்தைநின்","tr":"lattainiṉ","foot":"tēmāṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"லத்","tr":"lat"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"தை","tr":"tai"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"நின்","tr":"niṉ"}]},{"text":"குறியிருந்","tr":"kuṟiyirun","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"குறி","tr":"kuṟi"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"யிருந்","tr":"yirun"}]},{"text":"தோரே","tr":"tōrē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"தோ","tr":"tō"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ரே","tr":"rē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"உள்ளாற்று","parts":[{"text":"உள்","lemma":"உள்","gloss":"inside"},{"text":"ஆற்று","lemma":"ஆறு","gloss":"path (oblique)"}],"gloss":"of the inner path"},{"surface":"கவலை","parts":[{"text":"கவலை","lemma":"கவலை","gloss":"fork in a path"}],"gloss":"fork in a path"},{"surface":"புள்ளி","parts":[{"text":"புள்ளி","lemma":"புள்ளி","gloss":"dot/spot"}],"gloss":"dotted/dappled"},{"surface":"நீழல்","parts":[{"text":"நீழல்","lemma":"நீழல்","gloss":"shade"}],"gloss":"shade"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"முழூஉ","parts":[{"text":"முழூஉ","lemma":"முழூஉ","gloss":"entire/whole"}],"gloss":"entire/whole","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வள்ளுரம்","parts":[{"text":"வள்","lemma":"வள்","gloss":"strong/thick"},{"text":"உரம்","lemma":"உரம்","gloss":"flesh/strength"}],"gloss":"thick flesh"},{"surface":"உணக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"உணக்கு","lemma":"உணக்கு","gloss":"dry"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"drying"},{"surface":"மள்ள","parts":[{"text":"மள்ள","lemma":"மள்ள","gloss":"O warrior!"}],"gloss":"O warrior!","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புலவுதி","parts":[{"text":"புலவு","lemma":"புலவு","gloss":"sulk"},{"text":"தி","lemma":"தி","gloss":"you (second person singular suffix)"}],"gloss":"you are sulking"},{"surface":"மாதோ","parts":[{"text":"மாதோ","lemma":"மாதோ","gloss":"expletive particle"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"நீயே","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"you indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பலரால்","parts":[{"text":"பலர்","lemma":"பலர்","gloss":"many people"},{"text":"ஆல்","lemma":"ஆல்","gloss":"indeed (particle)"}],"gloss":"many indeed"},{"surface":"அத்தை","parts":[{"text":"அத்தை","lemma":"அத்தை","gloss":"expletive particle"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"குறி","parts":[{"text":"குறி","lemma":"குறி","gloss":"aim/presence"}],"gloss":"presence/sign"},{"surface":"இருந்தோரே","parts":[{"text":"இருந்தோர்","lemma":"இருந்தோர்","gloss":"those who sat"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"those who sat indeed"}]}],"literal":"In the dotted shade of the fork of the inner path / O warrior who dries the whole thick flesh! / You are indeed sulking / Indeed, many are those who sat waiting for your sign!","translation":"O warrior who dries your entire thick flesh in the dappled shade of the fork of the inner path! You are indeed sulking. But those who sat waiting for your sign to die with you are indeed many!","modern":"உள்ளே செல்லும் வழியின் கவர்த்த வழியில் உள்ள புள்ளிகளையுடைய நிழலில், உன்னுடைய முழுமையான தசைப்பற்றை உண்ணாநோன்பிருந்து காயவைக்கும் வீரனே! நீ பிணங்கி இருக்கிறாய். ஆனால், உன்னுடைய குறிப்பறிந்து உன்னோடு வடக்கிருக்க அமர்ந்தவர்கள் பலர் ஆவர்!","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Potuviyal tiṇai and Kaiyaṟunilai tuṟai, composed by Peruṅkaruvūrccatukkattu Pūtanātaṉār, addressed to Kōpperuñcōḻaṉ. The king, deeply hurt by the rebellion of his sons, decided to end his life by the ritual of fasting facing north (vaṭakkiruttal). The poet addresses the king as a warrior who is drying his flesh through fasting in the dappled shade of a path's fork. He notes that the king is sulking or aggrieved by his sons' behavior, which led him to this extreme step. However, the poet comforts him by pointing out that he is not alone, as many loyal friends and poets have also sat down to fast and die along with him, showing their deep love and solidarity.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}